**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** The run law walks every element of the light path, in light order, through its Mueller matrix, and starts from a real source whose default parameter set reproduces today's charts (001 §N 'The run law walks any number of objects. ExperimentRun folds slot by slot, in light order, through each item's Mueller matrix'; 'The source is real … "Unpolarized, unit scale after the first polarizer" is its default parameter set, so existing charts keep their values'; 001 §R: the 'first polarizer sets unit intensity' special case is removed; the S8.1 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, its module doc rewritten in one to three lines citing spec 0046 and spec 0050 S8.1, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (a) `RunStep` = `ElementStep of mueller : MuellerMatrix` (an element that is not an object, already evaluated at its orientation: a polarizer today, any prep or analyzer item from S8.2) | `ObjectStep of mueller : MuellerMatrix` (an object, already solved for the branch the detector's path leaves it by), with `member this.mueller : MuellerMatrix`. `PolarizerStep` and `SampleStep` are deleted, and a run holds any number of objects. (b) On `SourceEmission` (step 246): `member this.emittedInto (steps : RunStep list) : StokesVector` is `this.stokes` times the path's intensity reference r. For the first `ElementStep` in front of the first `ObjectStep` (the first element of a path with no object), r is the inverse of the S₀ its matrix passes of `Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`, when that S₀ is above zero; otherwise r is 1. So the intensity scale is referenced after the first polarizer, 001 §N's default: unpolarized light of unit scale leaves an ideal polarizer at unit S₀ exactly as `Propagation.inputStokes` gave it (an ideal matrix passes ½, so r is 2 and every product is exact), and a path with no element in front of its first object starts from the source's own state. (c) `detectorStokes (emission : SourceEmission) (steps : RunStep list) : StokesVector` folds `step.mueller * sv` over the steps from `emission.emittedInto steps`, and `read (kind : DetectorKind) (emission : SourceEmission) (steps : RunStep list) : Reading` reads it as today. The fold's `(StokesVector * bool * bool)` state and its first-polarizer arm (`ExperimentRun.fs:detectorStokes`) are deleted. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Propagation.fs`: `behaviorInputStokes` (`Propagation.fs:behaviorInputStokes`) is deleted with its doc, its last consumers going in this step; `inputStokes` and `unpolarizedStokes` stay, because `PropagationTests` builds its inputs from them. `DetectorIntensity`'s doc says the intensity is relative to the source's intensity reference (spec 0050 S8.1). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs` the `PolarizerBehavior` doc says `ComputedIdeal` evaluates through `Propagation.analyzerMueller`, no longer naming `inputStokes`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `model.runInputStokes` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runInputStokes`), which nothing reads, is deleted. (b) `chartForRun` builds every step through the evaluator (steps 247 and 249). A polarizer element bound to a preset is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`, evaluated per point at `{ rotation = its R1, or the swept x when its R1 is varied; incidence = IncidenceAngle.normal; branch = the path step's branch }`, as an `ElementStep`. A sample element bound to a library sample is bound once per path step by `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample model.materials (ParameterValues.defaultsOf sample.parameterAxes) sample`, so its materials are resolved once as today, and evaluated per point at `{ rotation = its spin (R1, or the swept x); incidence = its drawn incidence, or the swept x under VaryR2; branch = the path step's branch }` and the point's wavelength, as an `ObjectStep`. Every sample on the detector's `BeamLayout` path is solved, each for its own branch, as today. `StepBuilder`'s swept arm answers `Result<RunStep, ItemEvaluationError>`. (c) Every chart reads with `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` (step 244), the default parameter set, whatever source preset is bound, because a preset carries no parameter values; S8.2's source slot gives a source item's own values through `emissionWith` (step 246). (d) A `SampleMaterialErr e` keeps today's failure chart, title `Sample materials failed to resolve` and description `e.runFailureCaption` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runFailureCaption`); any other evaluation error, which the host's own inputs never raise, shows the title `The run cannot be evaluated` and its `describe`. (e) The docs of `chartForRun` and of the run section's header say what the law now is, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (4) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path': its clause 'polarizers before the sample prepare the input (the first sets a unit-intensity state), the sample acts at its drawn incidence and spin (its R1), polarizers after it analyze' becomes: every element on the path acts in light order through its Mueller matrix from `ItemEvaluation` (a polarizer at its R1, every sample at its drawn incidence and spin for the branch the path leaves it by), and the source emits its own Stokes state times its intensity scale, by default unpolarized with the unit scale after the first polarizer. Nothing else in the file changes. Every chart's numbers are unchanged, so `FsxAcceptanceTests` and the chart classes run as they are. Tests. `ExperimentRunTests`: its `lp` helper becomes `ElementStep (Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear θ)`, `clear` becomes `ObjectStep Propagation.identityMueller`, and every fact reads through a file-local default emission (`SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)`). `the source's light is unpolarized; the first polarizer sets a unit-intensity polarized input` becomes `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale, referenced after the first polarizer`, its assertions kept; `a polarizer AFTER the sample analyzes: crossed polarizers around a clear sample pass nothing` and `an ellipsometer reads Psi and Delta of the arriving state` keep their numbers over the new steps. New: `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`: for each ideal kind at 0°, 15°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°, 120°, 135°, 180°, 225°, 270°, 315° and 330°, the paths [prep], [prep; clear], [prep; clear; ideal LP at 60°], [prep; ideal LP at 90°], [clear; ideal LP at 60°] and [] read exactly the old rule's value written through the kept primitives (`inputStokes kind θ` with a prep and `unpolarizedStokes` without, then each later matrix), every component equal, because the products are exact. `objects in series apply their matrices in light order`: with a prep LP at 0°, the objects `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (30°) (Retardance (π / 2))` then `retarderMueller (75°) (Retardance (π / 3))` and an analyzer LP at 45°, `detectorStokes` equals A · M₂ · M₁ · `inputStokes IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and swapping the two objects changes S₀ by more than 1e-3. `a real source emits its own state times its scale`: a source of degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° and scale 2 reads 2 · [1, cos 60°, sin 60°, 0] through no element, and S₀ = 4 through an ideal LP at 30°, the reference being that first polarizer's unpolarized throughput (r = 2). `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other` : `ElementStep (Propagation.behaviorMueller (ConstantMueller [ { matrix = analyzerMueller IdealLinear (0°); offset = 0° } ]) (30°))` with the default source reads [1, cos 60°, sin 60°, 0] within 1e-12. `PolarizerBehaviorTests`: `behaviorInputStokes of a ComputedIdeal equals inputStokes across kinds and orientations` is deleted, its parity being `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`'s, and `behaviorInputStokes applies a constant compound to unpolarized light un-normalized` is deleted, `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other` pinning the new rule; every other fact is unchanged. `ExperimentControlsTests` (UI): `two bound samples in series are both solved on the detector's path`: over `initMain ()`, two samples added and bound through the file's `bind` helper to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id`, untilted on the main beam in front of the seeded intensity detector; the film chosen with `VaryR2` over 0 … 60° in 7 points and capture T: the series' value at each x equals the S₀ of the two transmitted `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` matrices (the plate at normal incidence, the film at x, spin 0, 600 nm, each resolved through the model's `materials`) applied to `unpolarizedStokes` in the order the detector's `BeamLayout` path lists them, within 1e-12.

**Acceptance.** After the run law lands, `ExperimentRun` MUST fold every step of the path through its Mueller matrix from the source's emission, with no first-polarizer arm, the default source MUST reproduce every existing reading exactly, and the host MUST build its steps through the item evaluator; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale, referenced after the first polarizer`, `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`, `objects in series apply their matrices in light order`, `a real source emits its own state times its scale` and `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other`, the count rising by 2 (four new facts, two `behaviorInputStokes` facts deleted); ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `two bound samples in series are both solved on the detector's path`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
